IMPORT prelude

-- Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 (Western Australia), Part 2 Division 1 -- licensing of vehicles -- with the Road Traffic
-- (Vehicles) Regulations 2014 that set its classes, periods, ages and charges, the Road Traffic (Administration)
-- Regulations 2014 that set its infringement penalties, and the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 provisions
-- that tie compulsory third party insurance to the vehicle licence.
--
-- SEAT: the vehicle owner. Every decision is phrased as the owner would ask it: "Must my car be licensed?", "Does my
-- e-bike or eRideable need a licence?", "Am I committing an offence driving it unlicensed, and what can it cost me?",
-- "I have sold my car -- what must I do, and by when?", "I have bought one -- what must I do, and what does the transfer
-- cost?", "Is my car covered by compulsory third party insurance?". Where the law hands a judgment to the CEO (of the
-- Department of Transport) or a court -- whether the vehicle meets the standards, where it is kept, whether there was "good
-- reason" -- that judgment is asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered. Act: s 3(1) ("light vehicle"); s 4 (vehicle licences and the offence of using an unlicensed vehicle);
-- s 5(1), (3) (application for grant or transfer, and when the CEO must transfer); s 7(1), (2) (recording and transfer
-- fees); s 10(1), (2), (6), (7) (the seller's and the buyer's notices, and failing to apply for transfer). Road Traffic
-- (Vehicles) Regulations 2014: r 3 ("motor vehicle", "car", "bicycle", "electric rideable device", "motorised scooter"),
-- r 15 (vehicles required to be licensed), r 16 (15 days' grace), r 21 (minimum age), r 30(1) (renewal period), r 31(1)
-- (periods of grant), r 51 (licence document handed over on disposal), r 54(1)-(3), r 54A, r 57 (charge for a car), r 99(1)
-- (recording fee), r 100 (transfer fee). Road Traffic (Administration) Regulations 2014: r 4 (power of a power assisted
-- pedal cycle), r 22 (infringement penalties for s 4(2), s 10(1), (2), (6)). Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008: s 4
-- ("power assisted pedal cycle", "motor vehicle"), s 6(2), (3) (who is the "responsible person"), s 7 (PU = $50). Motor
-- Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943: s 4(3A), (3B), (8), (8A), s 20(1), s 21 (the CTP link).
--
-- Edition. Act: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47806, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47806.txt; no compilation number stated; its compilation table ends with the Road
-- Traffic Legislation Amendment (Infringement Management Reform) Act 2024 Pt. 4 Div. 6 (No. 15 of 2024, in force 7 October
-- 2024). Road Traffic (Vehicles) Regulations 2014: version 01-av0-00, currency start 2 October 2026 (mrdoc 49887), deposited
-- at ../../../road-traffic-vehicles-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49887.txt. Road Traffic (Administration)
-- Regulations 2014: version 00-ay0-00, currency start 9 July 2026 (mrdoc 49740), deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-administration-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49740.txt. Road Traffic
-- (Administration) Act 2008 s 4, 6, 7 only (mrdoc 48196, retrieved 7 September 2026), deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-administration-act-2008/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48196.txt. Motor Vehicle (Third Party
-- Insurance) Act 1943 s 4, 20, 21 only (mrdoc 47506, retrieved 7 September 2026), deposited at
-- ../../../motor-vehicle-third-party-insurance-act-1943/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47506.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 6 (renewal regulations) beyond the grace period; s 7(3)-(6) beyond the car charge; s 8 (dishonoured
-- cheques); s 9 (cancellation and suspension) beyond treating a suspended or cancelled licence as not current; s 11, 12
-- (security declarations, change of nominated owner); s 13 beyond the permit and trade-plate defences; s 14 to s 19B
-- (register, labels, FPINE suspension orders, classes, inspection orders, offensive advertisements); Parts 3 to 12 (overseas
-- vehicles, mass, dimension and loading, defect notices, container weights, heavy vehicle sanctions) except s 131 is noted
-- below; heavy vehicle, motor cycle, trailer and other charges (r 58 to r 67); exemptions and concessions (r 68 to r 85,
-- including pensioners); examination fees; the vehicle licence duty itself (Duties Act 2008 Chapter 5, asked as a dollar
-- input); the CTP premium (set by the Insurance Commission, asked as a dollar input); what the CTP policy covers.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the vehicle owner, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 (WA), Part 2 -- licensing of vehicles`

§§ `helpers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- "per 100 kg, or part of 100 kg": the number of 100 kg blocks, rounding any part block up.
GIVEN `kg` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`hundreds of kg or part` MEANS
    IF TRUNC (`kg` DIVIDED BY 100) 0 EQUALS `kg` DIVIDED BY 100
    THEN TRUNC (`kg` DIVIDED BY 100) 0
    ELSE TRUNC (`kg` DIVIDED BY 100) 0 PLUS 1

-- Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 7: "a reference to a number of PU is a reference to an amount (in dollars) that
-- is that number multiplied by 50." This Act's s 3(2) sends the reader to that Act's Part 1 Division 2 for its terms.
@export How many dollars is a fine or infringement penalty of this many penalty units (Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 7)?
GIVEN `penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of penalty units (PU)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many dollars is this many penalty units` IS `penalty units` TIMES 50

§§ `s 4(1); Vehicles Regulations r 3, r 15; Administration Act s 4; Administration Regulations r 4 -- must my vehicle be licensed`

-- Kinds of vehicle, as the owner would describe them. The Regulations' own terms (r 3): "motor vehicle means a vehicle to be
-- propelled by a motor that forms part of the vehicle"; "trailer means a vehicle without its own motive power that is
-- built to be towed, or is towed, by a motor vehicle"; "bicycle", "electric rideable device" and "motorised scooter" take
-- their meanings from the Road Traffic Code 2000 (r 3(1), r 3A) -- borrowed terms, so asked as facts here (the Road Traffic
-- Act 1974 baseline works out r 3A from a device's specifications).
DECLARE `Kind of vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `a self-propelled motor vehicle such as a car, motor cycle, bus or truck`
    `a trailer`
    `a bicycle with an auxiliary motor (an e-bike)`
    `a bicycle without a motor`
    `an electric rideable device`
    `a motorised scooter`
    `a vehicle declared an electric personal transporter under Code r 230B`

DECLARE `My vehicle` HAS
    `what it is`                                                         IS A `Kind of vehicle`
    `it is designed so that it cannot go faster than 10 km/h`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an agricultural implement towed by a licensed or permitted vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is being towed by a licensed or permitted tow truck`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is designed to be propelled by human power through its pedals`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a pedalec meeting EN 15194`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `combined maximum output of its motors in watts`                     IS A NUMBER
    `its GVM in kg`                                                      IS A NUMBER

-- Administration Act s 4: "power assisted pedal cycle means a vehicle -- (a) designed to be propelled through a mechanism
-- operated solely by human power; and (b) to which is attached one or more auxiliary propulsion motors having a combined
-- maximum output not exceeding the amount of power prescribed". Administration Regulations r 4(2): "(a) for a pedalec --
-- 250 W; and (b) for any other kind of power assisted pedal cycle -- 200 W." r 4(1): "pedalec means a vehicle that meets
-- the standard ... EN 15194".
@export Is my e-bike a power assisted pedal cycle (Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 4; Administration Regulations r 4)?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your e-bike: whether it is pedal-driven, whether it meets EN 15194, and its motors' combined output
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my e-bike a power assisted pedal cycle` IF
        `the vehicle`'s `it is designed to be propelled by human power through its pedals`
    AND `the vehicle`'s `combined maximum output of its motors in watts` AT MOST
            (IF `the vehicle`'s `it is a pedalec meeting EN 15194` THEN 250 ELSE 200)

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an e-bike` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`'s `what it is`
    WHEN `a bicycle with an auxiliary motor (an e-bike)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Licensing answer` IS ONE OF
    `a vehicle licence is required: it is a motor vehicle or trailer (r 15(1))`
    `no licence: an agricultural implement towed by a licensed or permitted vehicle (r 15(2)(a))`
    `no licence: towed by a licensed or permitted tow truck (r 15(2)(b))`
    `no licence: a motor vehicle designed not to exceed 10 km/h (r 15(2)(c))`
    `no licence: a declared electric personal transporter (r 15(2)(d))`
    `no licence: a motorised scooter or electric rideable device (r 15(2)(e))`
    `no licence: a power assisted pedal cycle is a bicycle, not a motor vehicle (encoder's reading)`
    `no licence: not a motor vehicle or trailer`

-- s 4(1): "A vehicle licence is required for a vehicle of a prescribed class." r 15(1): "For section 4(1), a vehicle
-- licence is required for a vehicle that is a motor vehicle or a trailer." (2): "However, a vehicle licence is not required
-- for a motor vehicle or trailer that is -- (a) an agricultural implement being towed on a road by another vehicle in
-- respect of which a licence or permit under section 13(1) has been granted and is current; or (b) an unlicensed vehicle of
-- any type being towed on a road by a tow truck in respect of which a licence or permit ... is current; or (c) a motor
-- vehicle that is designed so as not to be capable of a speed exceeding 10 km/h; or (d) a vehicle declared as an electric
-- personal transporter under the Road Traffic Code 2000 regulation 230B; or (e) a motorised scooter or electric rideable
-- device."
-- The e-bike. r 15(2) does not name a power assisted pedal cycle. The encoder reads one as outside r 15(1) because it is not
-- a "motor vehicle": the Administration Act s 4 definition of "motor vehicle" (b)(ii) "does not include a power assisted
-- pedal cycle"; the Code's "bicycle", which r 3 adopts, "includes ... power assisted pedal cycle"; and the Regulations deal
-- with bicycles in Part 11, apart from motor vehicles in Part 10 (r 228(c)). INFERENCE: r 3's own "motor vehicle" ("a
-- vehicle to be propelled by a motor that forms part of the vehicle") could be read to catch it. A pedal bicycle whose motor
-- is over the limit is not a power assisted pedal cycle, is self-propelled, and is read as a motor vehicle that must be
-- licensed (INFERENCE, on the same definitions).
@export What does the law say about licensing my vehicle (s 4(1); Vehicles Regulations r 15)?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your vehicle: what it is, how fast it can go, whether it is being towed, and for an e-bike its pedals and motor
GIVETH A `Licensing answer`
DECIDE `What does the law say about licensing my vehicle` IS
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`'s `what it is`
    WHEN `a bicycle without a motor` THEN `no licence: not a motor vehicle or trailer`
    WHEN `an electric rideable device` THEN `no licence: a motorised scooter or electric rideable device (r 15(2)(e))`
    WHEN `a motorised scooter` THEN `no licence: a motorised scooter or electric rideable device (r 15(2)(e))`
    WHEN `a vehicle declared an electric personal transporter under Code r 230B` THEN `no licence: a declared electric personal transporter (r 15(2)(d))`
    WHEN `a trailer` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the vehicle`'s `it is an agricultural implement towed by a licensed or permitted vehicle`
               THEN `no licence: an agricultural implement towed by a licensed or permitted vehicle (r 15(2)(a))`
               IF `the vehicle`'s `it is being towed by a licensed or permitted tow truck`
               THEN `no licence: towed by a licensed or permitted tow truck (r 15(2)(b))`
               OTHERWISE `a vehicle licence is required: it is a motor vehicle or trailer (r 15(1))`
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH IF `is an e-bike` `the vehicle` AND `Is my e-bike a power assisted pedal cycle` `the vehicle`
               THEN `no licence: a power assisted pedal cycle is a bicycle, not a motor vehicle (encoder's reading)`
               IF `the vehicle`'s `it is being towed by a licensed or permitted tow truck`
               THEN `no licence: towed by a licensed or permitted tow truck (r 15(2)(b))`
               IF `the vehicle`'s `it is designed so that it cannot go faster than 10 km/h`
               THEN `no licence: a motor vehicle designed not to exceed 10 km/h (r 15(2)(c))`
               OTHERWISE `a vehicle licence is required: it is a motor vehicle or trailer (r 15(1))`

@export Must my vehicle be licensed (s 4(1); Vehicles Regulations r 15)?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your vehicle
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my vehicle be licensed` IF
    CONSIDER `What does the law say about licensing my vehicle` `the vehicle`
    WHEN `a vehicle licence is required: it is a motor vehicle or trailer (r 15(1))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 3(1): "light vehicle means a vehicle with a GVM of 4.5 t or less".
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a light vehicle` MEANS `the vehicle`'s `its GVM in kg` AT MOST 4500

§§ `s 4(2)-(6); Vehicles Regulations r 16, r 30(1) -- the offence of using an unlicensed vehicle`

DECLARE `Licence status` IS ONE OF
    `granted and current`
    `expired`
    `never granted`
    `suspended, cancelled or of no effect`

DECLARE `The use` HAS
    `it was used on a road, and I am its responsible person or I used it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licence`                                                        IS A `Licence status`
    `days since the licence expired`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `it was used under and in accordance with a s 13(1) permit`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was used with s 13(2) number plates and their requirements`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `its use is authorised under the law of another jurisdiction`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a responsible person for it is ordinarily resident in WA`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(3): no offence "arising out of the use of a vehicle within a period after the expiry of the licence that is -- (a)
-- prescribed by regulations made under section 6(2)(b) as a period within which the licence may be renewed; and (b)
-- prescribed for the purposes of this subsection." r 30(1): the renewal period ends "3 months after the day on which the
-- licence expired"; r 16: "For section 4(3)(b), the period after the expiry of the licence is 15 days." So 15 days.
GIVEN `the use` IS A `The use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is within the days of grace` MEANS
        `the use`'s `the licence` EQUALS `expired`
    AND `the use`'s `days since the licence expired` AT MOST 15

-- s 4(2)(b): "a licence has not been granted in respect of the vehicle or a licence has been granted ... but is not
-- current". A suspended licence is "of no effect" while suspended (s 16(1), (2A)); one bought by a dishonoured cheque "has no
-- effect" (s 8(1)). The encoder reads each as not current.
GIVEN `the use` IS A `The use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licence is not current` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the use`'s `the licence`
    WHEN `granted and current` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4(2): "A responsible person for a vehicle and each person who uses the vehicle on a road commits an offence if, at the
-- time the vehicle is used on the road -- (a) a vehicle licence is required for the vehicle; and (b) a licence has not been
-- granted ... or ... is not current." (3): the days of grace. (4): not "(a) under and in accordance with a permit issued
-- under section 13(1); or (b) with number plates mentioned in section 13(2) and in accordance with each requirement". (5):
-- not "while its use on a road is authorised under the law of another jurisdiction unless a responsible person for the
-- vehicle is ordinarily resident within this State."
@export Do I commit the offence of using an unlicensed vehicle on a road (s 4(2)-(5))?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your vehicle
      `the use` IS A `The use` @desc The use on a road: whether you are its responsible person or used it, the state of its licence and days since expiry, and any permit, trade plates or interstate authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit the offence of using an unlicensed vehicle` IF
        `the use`'s `it was used on a road, and I am its responsible person or I used it`
    AND `Must my vehicle be licensed` `the vehicle`
    AND `the licence is not current` `the use`
    AND (NOT `is within the days of grace` `the use`)
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `it was used under and in accordance with a s 13(1) permit`)
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `it was used with s 13(2) number plates and their requirements`)
    AND (NOT (    `the use`'s `its use is authorised under the law of another jurisdiction`
              AND (NOT `the use`'s `a responsible person for it is ordinarily resident in WA`)))

-- s 4(6): "A person is not to be convicted of an offence under subsection (2) if the person has already been convicted of,
-- or charged with and acquitted of, an offence under the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 section 4(3A), and
-- both those offences or alleged offences were committed simultaneously." The MVTPI Act s 4(3B) is the mirror image.
@export Can I be convicted of using an unlicensed vehicle (s 4(2), (6))?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your vehicle
      `the use` IS A `The use` @desc The use on a road
      `I have already been convicted or acquitted of the uninsured-vehicle offence for the same use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been convicted of, or charged with and acquitted of, the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 s 4(3A) offence for the same use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be convicted of using an unlicensed vehicle` IF
        `Do I commit the offence of using an unlicensed vehicle` `the vehicle` `the use`
    AND (NOT `I have already been convicted or acquitted of the uninsured-vehicle offence for the same use`)

§§ `s 4(2) penalty; Administration Regulations r 22 -- what it can cost me`

-- s 4(2): "Penalty: a fine of 10 PU, and in addition, the court is to order the accused to pay a further penalty equal to
-- the charges payable under this Act for the grant of a vehicle licence for the vehicle concerned for a period of 6 months."
@export What fine does s 4(2) set for using an unlicensed vehicle, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fine is set for using an unlicensed vehicle` IS `How many dollars is this many penalty units` 10

-- r 54(2): "The vehicle licence charge payable for a vehicle for a period of 6 months is one-half of the charge payable for
-- that vehicle for a period of one year." The encoder reads "the charges payable ... for the grant" as the vehicle licence
-- charge (s 7(3)) and not the recording fee (s 7(1)), which the Act calls a "fee" (INFERENCE).
@export What further penalty must the court order on top of the fine for using an unlicensed vehicle (s 4(2); r 54(2))?
GIVEN `the annual vehicle licence charge` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle licence charge for one year for the vehicle, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What further penalty must the court order` IS `the annual vehicle licence charge` DIVIDED BY 2

@export What can a court make me pay for using my unlicensed car on a road (s 4(2); r 54(2), r 57)?
GIVEN `tare in kg` IS A NUMBER @desc Your car's tare (unladen mass), in kg, as the manufacturer specifies it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What can a court make me pay for using my unlicensed car` IS
    `What fine is set for using an unlicensed vehicle` PLUS `What further penalty must the court order` (`What is my car's annual vehicle licence charge` `tare in kg`)

-- Administration Regulations r 22, Table: "s. 4(2) Using on a road a light vehicle that does not have the requisite, or a
-- current, licence 5" PU. Only a light vehicle is listed, so a heavy vehicle's s 4(2) offence goes to court.
@export Can my unlicensed-vehicle offence be dealt with by an infringement notice (Administration Regulations r 22)?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your vehicle, with its GVM
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can it be dealt with by infringement notice` IF `is a light vehicle` `the vehicle`

@export What is the infringement notice penalty for using my unlicensed light vehicle, in dollars (Administration Regulations r 22)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the infringement penalty for an unlicensed light vehicle` IS `How many dollars is this many penalty units` 5

§§ `r 31(1), r 54, r 54A, r 57, r 99(1) -- what licensing my car costs`

-- r 57: "For a car or bus, a goods vehicle or a motor home the charge is $13.20 plus $29.76 per 100 kg, or part of 100 kg,
-- of tare, subject to a maximum charge of $586.00." (Subdivision 2: vehicles other than heavy vehicles, r 55.)
@export What is my car's vehicle licence charge for one year (Vehicles Regulations r 57)?
GIVEN `tare in kg` IS A NUMBER @desc Your car's tare (unladen mass), in kg
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my car's annual vehicle licence charge` IS
    `the lesser of` (13.20 PLUS 29.76 TIMES `hundreds of kg or part` `tare in kg`) 586

-- r 31(1): a licence is granted for "a period of 1 year, 6 months or 3 months" as the applicant elects. r 54(2), (3): 6
-- months is "one-half", 3 months "one-quarter" of the one-year charge. r 54A(1): on an election for 1 year for a vehicle
-- other than a heavy vehicle, "the charge for the grant or renewal is reduced by $6.60".
DECLARE `Licence period` IS ONE OF `1 year`, `6 months`, `3 months`

@export What is my car's vehicle licence charge for the period I choose (Vehicles Regulations r 31(1), r 54, r 54A)?
GIVEN `tare in kg` IS A NUMBER @desc Your car's tare, in kg
      `the period` IS A `Licence period` @desc The period you choose: 1 year, 6 months or 3 months
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my car's vehicle licence charge for the period` IS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `1 year`   THEN `What is my car's annual vehicle licence charge` `tare in kg` MINUS 6.60
    WHEN `6 months` THEN `What is my car's annual vehicle licence charge` `tare in kg` DIVIDED BY 2
    WHEN `3 months` THEN `What is my car's annual vehicle licence charge` `tare in kg` DIVIDED BY 4

-- s 7(1): "The prescribed recording fee is to be paid ... for the grant, renewal or variation of any licence"; r 99(1): "a
-- recording fee of $9.70" (other amounts apply to renewals paid by direct debit, r 99(1A), not encoded). MVTPI Act s 4(8):
-- "no licence is to be granted or renewed ... unless, before or at the time of the grant or renewal, there is paid ... the
-- appropriate insurance premium determined by the Commission" -- the premium is set outside these instruments, so asked.
@export What will I pay to license (or renew) my car for the period I choose, including the CTP premium (r 54, r 54A, r 57, r 99(1); MVTPI Act s 4(8))?
GIVEN `tare in kg` IS A NUMBER @desc Your car's tare, in kg
      `the period` IS A `Licence period` @desc The period you choose
      `the CTP premium for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The compulsory third party insurance premium the Insurance Commission has set for your class of vehicle and the period, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What will I pay to license my car` IS
    `What is my car's vehicle licence charge for the period` `tare in kg` `the period` PLUS 9.70 PLUS `the CTP premium for the period`

§§ `s 5(1), (3); r 21, r 100 -- buying a vehicle: having the licence transferred to me`

-- r 21: "The minimum age at which an individual may apply for the grant or transfer of a vehicle licence for -- (a) a vehicle
-- that is not a heavy vehicle is 16 years; or (b) a heavy vehicle is 18 years." (r 12: a heavy vehicle has an MRC over
-- 4 500 kg -- asked as a fact.)
@export Am I old enough to apply for the grant or transfer of a vehicle licence (Vehicles Regulations r 21)?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
      `it is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a heavy vehicle (an MRC over 4 500 kg, r 12)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough to apply for a vehicle licence` IF
    `my age in years` AT LEAST (IF `it is a heavy vehicle` THEN 18 ELSE 16)

DECLARE `My transfer application` HAS
    `my age in years`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `it is a heavy vehicle`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have given the proof of age and identity the CEO requires`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have paid the transfer fee and the duty`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle meets the prescribed standards and is fit for its purpose, or is a prescribed exception` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have complied with the Duties Act 2008 on the transfer`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO is satisfied the vehicle is kept primarily in WA or in no jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another jurisdiction's law would prevent me holding a licence for it`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a fines enforcement order, immobilisation or plate removal affects the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a licence warning notice is in force for the vehicle`                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 5(1): "An owner of a vehicle may apply for the grant, renewal, transfer or variation of a licence ... by -- (a)
-- submitting an application in a form approved by the CEO; and (b) paying ... (i) any fee or charge ... required by
-- section 7; and (ii) the duty, and any penalty tax, payable under the Duties Act 2008". s 5(3): "the CEO must ...
-- transfer ... if -- (a) ... the vehicle meets the prescribed standards and requirements ... (b) ... the applicant has
-- attained any minimum age ... and provided any proof of age and identity ...; (c) the applicant has complied with any
-- applicable provisions of the Duties Act 2008 ...; (d) the CEO is satisfied that -- (i) the vehicle is kept primarily in
-- this State; or (ii) ... not kept primarily in any jurisdiction; (e) ... would not be prevented by or under the law of
-- another jurisdiction ...; (f)-(j) [no FPINE licence suspension order, immobilisation, plate removal, or vehicle licence
-- suspension or cancellation order]; ... (l) in the case of an application for the transfer of a licence -- there is no
-- licence warning notice relating to the vehicle in force." The CEO's satisfaction, and whether the vehicle meets the
-- standards, are asked as facts.
@export Must the CEO transfer the vehicle licence to me (s 5(1), (3); r 21, r 22)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My transfer application` @desc Your application: your age, proof of identity, payment, the vehicle's standards, where it is kept, and any orders or warning notices affecting it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the CEO transfer the licence to me` IF
        `the application`'s `I have paid the transfer fee and the duty`
    AND `the application`'s `the vehicle meets the prescribed standards and is fit for its purpose, or is a prescribed exception`
    AND `Am I old enough to apply for a vehicle licence` (`the application`'s `my age in years`) (`the application`'s `it is a heavy vehicle`)
    AND `the application`'s `I have given the proof of age and identity the CEO requires`
    AND `the application`'s `I have complied with the Duties Act 2008 on the transfer`
    AND `the application`'s `the CEO is satisfied the vehicle is kept primarily in WA or in no jurisdiction`
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `another jurisdiction's law would prevent me holding a licence for it`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `a fines enforcement order, immobilisation or plate removal affects the vehicle`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `a licence warning notice is in force for the vehicle`)

-- s 7(2): "The prescribed transfer fee is to be paid to the CEO for effecting the transfer"; r 100: "A fee of $20.50 is
-- payable in respect of the transfer of a vehicle licence." The duty is the Duties Act 2008's (not encoded here), asked.
-- No vehicle licence charge, recording fee or CTP premium is payable on a transfer: s 7(1), (3) and MVTPI s 4(8) speak of
-- grant, renewal and variation only.
@export What must I pay to have the licence transferred into my name (s 5(1)(b), s 7(2); r 100)?
GIVEN `the duty` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle licence duty (and any penalty tax) payable under the Duties Act 2008 on the transfer, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What must I pay to transfer the licence` IS 20.50 PLUS `the duty`

§§ `s 10(1), (2); r 51; Administration Act s 6 -- selling or buying: the notices, and by when`

DECLARE `My side of the sale` IS ONE OF `I sold it`, `I bought it`

-- s 10(1): "A person to whom a licence in respect of a vehicle has been granted must, within 7 days after ceasing to be the
-- owner of the vehicle -- (a) give notice in writing to the CEO of the name and address of the new owner". (2): "A person
-- who becomes the owner of a vehicle in respect of which a licence has been granted must, within 14 days after becoming the
-- owner, give notice in writing to the CEO of that fact." Each: "Penalty: a fine of 10 PU."
@export Within how many days of the sale must I notify the CEO in writing (s 10(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my side` IS A `My side of the sale` @desc Whether you sold or bought the licensed vehicle
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I notify the CEO` IS
    CONSIDER `my side`
    WHEN `I sold it` THEN 7
    WHEN `I bought it` THEN 14

-- The offence is complete when the deadline passes without the notice. The owner states the number of days after the sale
-- on which the notice was given, or, if none has been given, the number of days that have passed.
@export Have I committed the offence of not notifying the CEO of the sale in time (s 10(1)(a), (2))?
GIVEN `my side` IS A `My side of the sale` @desc Whether you sold or bought the licensed vehicle
      `days after the sale when I notified, or days so far if I have not` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after the change of ownership on which you gave written notice, or, if you have not, the number of days since it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I failed to notify the CEO in time` IF
    `days after the sale when I notified, or days so far if I have not` GREATER THAN `Within how many days must I notify the CEO` `my side`

-- s 10(1)(b): the seller must also "return the licence document and the related number plates to the CEO if -- (i) the
-- licence was granted free of charge or upon the payment of a reduced vehicle licence charge; and (ii) the vehicle licence
-- charge, or the difference ..., has not been paid."
@export When I sell, must I return the licence document and number plates to the CEO (s 10(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the licence was free or reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence was granted free of charge or at a reduced charge
      `the full charge or difference has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the full charge, or the difference, has since been paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I return the licence document and plates` IF
    `the licence was free or reduced` AND (NOT `the full charge or difference has been paid`)

-- Administration Regulations r 22: s 10(1) and s 10(2) may each be dealt with by an infringement notice of 2 PU.
@export What is the infringement notice penalty for not notifying the CEO of a sale in time, in dollars (Administration Regulations r 22)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the infringement penalty for a late sale notice` IS `How many dollars is this many penalty units` 2

-- r 51(2): "A person who ... disposes of a used licensed vehicle, must ensure that at the time of the disposal the new owner
-- ... is given the current licence document". (3): if "the licence for which has expired in the 3 month period before the
-- time of the disposal", "the most recent licence document". Modified penalty 2 PU each. Three months is asked as a fact.
@export When I sell my vehicle, must I hand the buyer its licence document (Vehicles Regulations r 51)?
GIVEN `the licence` IS A `Licence status` @desc The state of the vehicle's licence at the time of the sale
      `it expired within the 3 months before the sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it has expired: whether it expired within the 3 months before the sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I hand the buyer the licence document` IF
    CONSIDER `the licence`
    WHEN `granted and current` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `expired` THEN `it expired within the 3 months before the sale`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Administration Act s 6(2): "For the purposes of a road law a person responsible for a vehicle is -- (a) if the vehicle is
-- licensed -- any licence holder who has not given a notice as described in paragraph (b); or (b) if a licence holder has
-- given notice under the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 section 10(1) ... -- the new owner as specified in the notice".
-- (3): not the new owner "if it can be shown that the person did not agree to becoming an owner of the vehicle and has
-- notified the CEO in writing accordingly". So the seller's notice is what moves the s 4(2) liability to the buyer.
@export I have sold my licensed vehicle: am I still its "responsible person" (Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 6(2)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `I have given the CEO the s 10(1) notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the CEO written notice of the new owner's name and address
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still responsible for the vehicle I sold` IF (NOT `I have given the CEO the s 10(1) notice`)

@export I have bought a licensed vehicle: am I its "responsible person" (Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 6(2)(b), (3))?
GIVEN `the seller has notified the CEO naming me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller has given the CEO the s 10(1) notice naming you as the new owner
      `I did not agree to become the owner and have told the CEO in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not agree to becoming an owner and have notified the CEO in writing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I responsible for the vehicle I bought` IF
    `the seller has notified the CEO naming me` AND (NOT `I did not agree to become the owner and have told the CEO in writing`)

§§ `s 10(3)(b), (6), (7) -- the CEO's notice to apply for transfer`

DECLARE `The CEO's transfer notice` HAS
    `the CEO has issued me a notice to apply for transfer`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since the notice was issued`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `further days the CEO allowed beyond 28`                               IS A NUMBER
    `I have applied for the transfer`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I did not agree to become an owner and told the CEO in writing`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `another person has been nominated as owner`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court accepts there was good reason for not applying`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 10(6): "A person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (3)(b) commits an offence if an application for the transfer
-- of the licence for the vehicle is not made within 28 days after the notice is issued, or any longer period that the CEO
-- allows, unless it can be shown that -- (a) the person did not agree to becoming an owner ... and has notified the CEO in
-- writing accordingly; or (b) another person has been nominated ...; or (c) there is more than one owner ... and there is
-- good reason for not nominating ...; or (d) there was some other good reason ... Penalty: a fine of 50 PU." Whether a
-- reason under (c) or (d) is "good" is the court's judgment, asked as a fact.
@export Have I committed the offence of not applying for transfer after the CEO's notice (s 10(6))?
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `The CEO's transfer notice` @desc The CEO's notice: when it was issued, any extra time allowed, whether you applied, and any excuse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I failed to apply for transfer after the CEO's notice` IF
        `the notice`'s `the CEO has issued me a notice to apply for transfer`
    AND (NOT `the notice`'s `I have applied for the transfer`)
    AND `the notice`'s `days since the notice was issued` GREATER THAN (28 PLUS `the notice`'s `further days the CEO allowed beyond 28`)
    AND (NOT `the notice`'s `I did not agree to become an owner and told the CEO in writing`)
    AND (NOT `the notice`'s `another person has been nominated as owner`)
    AND (NOT `the notice`'s `the court accepts there was good reason for not applying`)

-- s 10(7): "The court convicting a person of an offence under subsection (6) must, whether imposing a penalty or not, order
-- the person to pay the sum of -- (a) the prescribed transfer fee; and (b) the amount payable under a taxation Act ... in
-- respect of the transfer of the licence."
@export If convicted of not applying for transfer, what most can a court make me pay (s 10(6), (7); r 100)?
GIVEN `the duty on the transfer` IS A NUMBER @desc The duty payable under the Duties Act 2008 on the transfer, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What most can a court make me pay for not applying for transfer` IS
    `How many dollars is this many penalty units` 50 PLUS 20.50 PLUS `the duty on the transfer`

§§ `MVTPI Act s 4(8A), s 20(1), s 21 -- is my vehicle covered by compulsory third party insurance`

DECLARE `CTP answer` IS ONE OF
    `insured: the CTP policy goes with the vehicle licence`
    `uninsured`
    `not decided here: a suspended, cancelled or void licence (see the MVTPI Act baseline)`

-- MVTPI s 4(8A): "The grant or renewal of a licence under the Vehicles Act in respect of a motor vehicle is to be taken to
-- constitute the issue of a policy of insurance complying with this Act -- (a) in respect of the motor vehicle; and (b) in
-- respect of the period for which the licence is granted or renewed." s 20(1): the policy "shall not be deemed to be
-- cancelled ... solely by reason of a change of ownership" and "shall ... enure in favour of every person who, during the
-- period ..., becomes an owner". s 21(2): if the licence "is renewed within the period of 15 days after the day on which
-- the vehicle licence expired, the operation of the policy ... is ... extended until the vehicle licence is renewed"; (4):
-- otherwise "the motor vehicle is an uninsured motor vehicle for the period beginning on the day after the day on which the
-- vehicle licence expired".
@export Is my motor vehicle covered by compulsory third party insurance (MVTPI Act s 4(8A), s 20(1), s 21)?
GIVEN `the licence` IS A `Licence status` @desc The state of the vehicle's licence
      `it was renewed within 15 days after it expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it has expired: whether it was (or will be) renewed within 15 days after the day it expired
GIVETH A `CTP answer`
DECIDE `Is my vehicle covered by CTP` IS
    CONSIDER `the licence`
    WHEN `granted and current` THEN `insured: the CTP policy goes with the vehicle licence`
    WHEN `expired` THEN
        IF `it was renewed within 15 days after it expired`
        THEN `insured: the CTP policy goes with the vehicle licence`
        ELSE `uninsured`
    WHEN `never granted` THEN `uninsured`
    OTHERWISE `not decided here: a suspended, cancelled or void licence (see the MVTPI Act baseline)`
